The workspace is Documents, not the palace inside it
====================================================

A new conversation opened on `~/Documents/memory-palace`, so every ordinary question about a file —
"what is in my Documents", "can I show you this" — was an access **outside** the workspace, and the
answer was a permission dialog. The palace lives inside Documents; the workspace default should be the
folder that contains both the palace and the person's other files.

The palace path is still what the memory system writes to. Only the default working folder changed.

diff -ruN '--exclude=target' '--exclude=.git' qtest17/QuixiDesk-3.6556.12/resources/ui/app.js qcur/QuixiDesk-3.6556.12/resources/ui/app.js
--- a/resources/ui/app.js	2026-11-02 21:41:19.558594050 -0800
+++ b/resources/ui/app.js	2026-11-02 21:52:39.639105260 -0800
@@ -4986,7 +4986,12 @@
     let info = null;
     try { info = await rpc("Memory", "info"); } catch {}
     const path = (info && (info.path || info.defaultPath)) || "";
-    palaceFolderCache = { path, dataDir: (info && info.dataDir) || "" };
+    // The workspace is the palace's PARENT, not the palace itself. A workspace of
+    // Documents/memory-palace makes every ordinary file question — "what is in my Documents" —
+    // an access-outside-the-workspace request, which is a permission prompt for something the
+    // person already considers theirs. Documents holds the palace and the rest of their files.
+    const parent = path && path.lastIndexOf("/") > 0 ? path.slice(0, path.lastIndexOf("/")) : path;
+    palaceFolderCache = { path: parent, palace: path, dataDir: (info && info.dataDir) || "" };
     return palaceFolderCache;
   }
 
